  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.1.2 - Added FakeValueGenerator.Create<T>() to create and populate a single fake instance, and Create<T>(numberToCreate) to create and populate multiple fake instances at once (using each item's index as the seed so predictable values are unique across the collection);\nv3.1 - Adding FakeValueGenerator to Benday.Common.Testing to streamline test data generation in tests; Added reflection-based assertions AssertThat.PropertiesAreEqual (compares two objects property-by-property, reporting all mismatches at once) and AssertThat.AllPropertiesAreNonNullAndNonDefaultValue (verifies every property holds a non-default value) -- companions to FakeValueGenerator; added optional per-property special-case callbacks to PropertiesAreEqual, AllPropertiesAreNonNullAndNonDefaultValue, and FakeValueGenerator.PopulateFakeValues;\nv3.0.4 - Adding fluent version of MockUtility create method so that you can refer to a specific method and provide specific values for scalars;\nv3.0.2 - Migrated from xunit v2 to xunit.v3;\nv3.0 - Major version bump: Added InMemoryTenantRepository and InMemoryReadableRepository for testing service layers without storage emulators; Added dependency on Benday.Common.Interfaces;\nv2.2.1 - Metadata updates only;\nv2.2 - Updated dependencies to include netstandard2.1;\nv2.1 - Updated dependencies to .net 10.0;\nv2.0 - Major overhaul of assertion methods so that they following a consistent naming pattern; Added new overloads to existing assertion methods to not require custom messages;\nv1.5 - Added assert utility methods;\nv1.4 - Changed the way MockUtility and MockCreationResult work to allow for optional mock configuration before instance creation;\nv1.3 - Unpublishing fluent assertions for xUnit from this package...for now;\nv1.2 - Added fluent assertions for xUnit to the package;\nv1.1 - Added base class functionality for reading sample data files during tests; Removed dependency on FluentAssertions;\nv1.0 - Base class for xunit tests; MockUtility for streamlining testing with Moq;",
